@startuml c4-dynamic-recall
!include ../vendor/style.puml
title Dynamic view — recall investigation, from scope to signed notice

autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 240
skinparam BoxPadding 8
skinparam participant {
  BackgroundColor #438DD5
  FontColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #2E6DA4
}
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #444444
  LifeLineBorderColor #999999
  GroupBorderColor #999999
  GroupHeaderFontColor #444444
}

participant "Regulator officer" as officer
participant "Traceability App" as app
participant "Workers" as workers
participant "Relayer" as relayer
participant "Evidence owner" as owner #999999
participant "External Archive" as archive #999999
participant "Public Blockchain" as chain #999999

== Phase 1 · Scope at a fixed watermark ==
officer -> app: Recall scope for lot L at watermark W
app -> app: Traverse transformation, aggregation and handover edges;\nkeep competing edges side by side
app --> officer: confirmedImpact + provisionalImpact, with provenance
note right of app: provisionalImpact covers receipted but\nunconfirmed claims; it is labelled and never merged

== Phase 2 · Human review and evidence ==
officer -> app: Evidence request for resource R
app -> owner: Evidence request recorded as an audit record
owner -> app: Content encrypted to the regulator key
app --> officer: Reference and commitment only;\nthe platform cannot read the content
note right of owner: The platform never sees plaintext.\nThe officer checks the content against\nthe salted commitment.

== Phase 3 · Formal notice ==
officer -> app: Submit signed Recall Notice
app -> workers: Record notice intent
workers -> archive: Write notice, obtain ArchiveAck
archive --> workers: Signed ArchiveAck
workers --> app: Ack digest recorded
app --> officer: Published as PENDING_ANCHOR
note right of app: Publication does not wait for finality,\nbut it is not presented as CONFIRMED.

== Phase 4 · Anchor and confirm ==
relayer -> chain: Commit notice in the next Merkle batch
chain --> relayer: Finality and inclusion proof
relayer --> app: Inclusion proof recorded
app --> officer: CONFIRMED

note over officer, chain: Recall starts from an external decision, not from the platform.\nThe platform produces the scope and carries the signed notice;\nit does not withdraw stock, and it does not decide who is at fault.

@enduml